WEBVTT

00:00:13.058 --> 00:00:14.435
This is a telescope.

00:00:14.602 --> 00:00:16.604
Old man Bernardi lets me use it.

00:00:16.687 --> 00:00:19.857
It makes faraway things seem close. Look.

00:00:22.651 --> 00:00:23.652
(LUCA GASPS IN AWE)

00:00:23.736 --> 00:00:25.321
GIULIA: See any fish?

00:00:25.404 --> 00:00:26.864
Then what are all those?

00:00:26.947 --> 00:00:28.657
Stars. Like the sun.

00:00:28.741 --> 00:00:30.910
Giant, raging balls of fire!

00:00:31.076 --> 00:00:32.995
So, Alberto was wrong.

00:00:33.078 --> 00:00:35.080
And stars are circled by planets.

00:00:38.626 --> 00:00:39.627
Look.

00:00:40.628 --> 00:00:42.505
That's Saturno. It's my favorite.

00:00:42.588 --> 00:00:44.423
It's the lightest of the planets.

00:00:44.507 --> 00:00:47.426
They say if there was an ocean
big enough to hold it,

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:48.719
it would float in it!

00:00:48.802 --> 00:00:50.012
Whoa!

00:00:50.095 --> 00:00:51.096
(GRUNTS)

00:00:52.264 --> 00:00:53.265
Wow!

00:00:53.349 --> 00:00:55.351
(ENTHRALLING MUSIC PLAYING)

00:00:57.186 --> 00:00:58.562
(GASPS IN AWE)

00:00:58.646 --> 00:01:00.022
GIULIA: Come on, Luca!

00:01:03.192 --> 00:01:05.194
(ENTHRALLING MUSIC CONTINUES)

00:01:10.199 --> 00:01:11.200
(GASPS)

00:01:11.283 --> 00:01:13.285
(ENTHRALLING MUSIC CONTINUES)

00:01:27.424 --> 00:01:28.509
LUCA: So, this is how machines fly?

00:01:28.592 --> 00:01:29.593
GIULIA: Sì.

00:01:29.677 --> 00:01:31.220
LUCA: And there are big towns
called cities?

00:01:31.303 --> 00:01:32.304
GIULIA: Sì.

00:01:32.388 --> 00:01:33.597
Like even bigger than Portorosso?

00:01:33.681 --> 00:01:35.850
Like Genova! Literally 20 times bigger.

00:01:35.933 --> 00:01:37.893
And we're all on a big round rock,

00:01:37.977 --> 00:01:39.270
floating around a star

00:01:39.353 --> 00:01:41.313
in the "solar system"?

00:01:41.397 --> 00:01:42.773
So cool, right?

00:01:42.857 --> 00:01:44.984
And is there anything
beyond the solar system?

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:47.528
Only a galaxy full of solar systems.

00:01:47.611 --> 00:01:50.156
-Then what?
-A universe full of galaxies!

00:01:50.239 --> 00:01:52.032
(LAUGHS EXCITEDLY)
And then what?

00:01:52.116 --> 00:01:53.450
And then...

00:01:53.784 --> 00:01:54.827
I don't know.

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:56.871
But next year in Advanced Astronomy,

00:01:56.954 --> 00:01:58.581
I'm gonna use my school's telescope.

00:01:58.664 --> 00:01:59.832
So, maybe I'll find out.

00:02:00.124 --> 00:02:03.043
That thing's huge.
I wish I could show it to you.

00:02:03.127 --> 00:02:05.713
Just promise you'll tell me
everything you see!

00:02:06.088 --> 00:02:07.590
Sorry. Too much?

00:02:07.673 --> 00:02:09.008
(LAUGHS) Never.

00:02:09.091 --> 00:02:10.092
(BOTH LAUGHING)

00:02:10.176 --> 00:02:12.094
Hey, Luca, I've been looking
everywhere for you.

00:02:12.178 --> 00:02:14.388
-LUCA: Oh, sorry.
-Just come on. Let's go.

00:02:14.555 --> 00:02:17.850
Could I maybe borrow this?
Just for tonight.

00:02:20.144 --> 00:02:21.437
GIULIA: You can have it.

00:02:23.189 --> 00:02:24.315
Ha-ha!

00:02:24.982 --> 00:02:27.776
The universe is literally yours!

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:29.320
Wow. Thank you!

00:02:29.403 --> 00:02:30.446
Luca!

00:02:30.529 --> 00:02:31.739
LUCA: Okay.

00:02:36.702 --> 00:02:37.703
LUCA: Where are we going?

00:02:37.786 --> 00:02:39.330
ALBERTO: Come on.
I got something to show you.

00:02:39.788 --> 00:02:43.083
Hey, you won't believe this.
Those aren't fish.

00:02:43.167 --> 00:02:44.210
-What?
-Yeah.

00:02:44.293 --> 00:02:45.669
Giulia explained it to me.

00:02:45.753 --> 00:02:46.754
They're fires.

00:02:46.837 --> 00:02:49.131
But, like, one million times bigger.

00:02:49.215 --> 00:02:50.925
Uh, no, they're not.

00:02:51.759 --> 00:02:52.843
(CAT MEOWS)

00:02:54.053 --> 00:02:57.014
(SIGHS) Soon you'll be ours, sweet Vespa.

00:02:57.181 --> 00:02:58.182
Take a look.

00:02:58.265 --> 00:03:00.226
I thought of every
single thing we're gonna need.

00:03:00.309 --> 00:03:01.560
Also, I added flames.

00:03:02.061 --> 00:03:03.521
That's so cool!

00:03:03.938 --> 00:03:06.524
Oh! And we can bring
a telescope, too!

00:03:06.607 --> 00:03:08.692
Yeah! That shoots lightning!

00:03:08.776 --> 00:03:09.777
LUCA: No, no, no.

00:03:09.944 --> 00:03:11.445
You look through it.

00:03:11.779 --> 00:03:14.865
Giulia says there's an even
bigger one at her school.

00:03:15.074 --> 00:03:16.951
Wait. What if we visit her there?

00:03:17.034 --> 00:03:18.828
Why would you wanna do that?

00:03:18.911 --> 00:03:20.621
It kinda sounds interesting.

00:03:20.704 --> 00:03:23.332
The whole reason we're getting a Vespa
is to live on our own.

00:03:23.415 --> 00:03:26.001
We don't need school.
We don't need anybody.

00:03:26.085 --> 00:03:28.045
Couldn't we just try it?

00:03:28.128 --> 00:03:29.672
Just for a few days?

00:03:29.755 --> 00:03:32.341
Luca, sea monsters can't go to school.

00:03:32.424 --> 00:03:33.884
What do you think is gonna happen

00:03:33.968 --> 00:03:35.386
when they see your fish face?

00:03:36.011 --> 00:03:37.012
(SIGHS)

00:03:37.596 --> 00:03:38.597
(GASPS)

00:03:38.681 --> 00:03:40.558
ERCOLE: Hey, look who it is.

00:03:40.641 --> 00:03:42.810
And with no Giulia to hide behind.

00:03:42.893 --> 00:03:44.520
-Come on. Let's go.
-No.

00:03:44.603 --> 00:03:46.522
Something's fishy with you two.

00:03:46.605 --> 00:03:48.190
-I mean, besides the smell.
-(LAUGHS)

00:03:48.274 --> 00:03:49.483
You're hiding something.

00:03:49.733 --> 00:03:51.652
Is it that we're smarter than you?

00:03:51.735 --> 00:03:53.737
I mean, we're not really hiding that.

00:03:53.821 --> 00:03:55.197
It's just kind of obvious.

00:03:55.281 --> 00:03:57.408
You know, people think I'm a nice guy.

00:03:57.491 --> 00:03:58.993
Always joking around.

00:03:59.076 --> 00:04:01.328
But really, I'm not.

00:04:01.412 --> 00:04:03.455
-Stop!
-Wait your turn, piccoletto.

00:04:03.539 --> 00:04:05.958
I want to make myself very clear.

00:04:06.041 --> 00:04:07.543
This is my town,

00:04:07.626 --> 00:04:08.752
-number one...
-(COUGHS)

00:04:08.836 --> 00:04:12.464
...and number two, I don't want you in it.

00:04:12.882 --> 00:04:14.341
I... I said stop!

00:04:14.717 --> 00:04:17.803
Put that down, piccoletto.
You'll hurt yourself.

00:04:17.887 --> 00:04:19.138
-LUCA: Let him go!
-(ALBERTO GRUNTS)

00:04:21.307 --> 00:04:24.727
Go. Now. Before I change my mind.

00:04:25.311 --> 00:04:29.023
Nobody wants you here, idioti!
Keep running!

00:04:30.232 --> 00:04:31.859
(BOTH PANTING)

00:04:31.942 --> 00:04:34.528
Why did you make him mad?
We should've left.

00:04:34.612 --> 00:04:36.030
No, no, no. We're fine.

00:04:36.405 --> 00:04:37.907
I had it under control.

00:04:38.073 --> 00:04:41.160
All you gotta do
is follow my lead, remember?

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:50.085
(MIMICKING BUGLE PLAYING WAKEUP CALL)

00:04:51.212 --> 00:04:52.713
-(GROANS)
-Rise and shine!

00:04:52.796 --> 00:04:54.507
(UPBEAT ITALIAN POP MUSIC PLAYING)

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:57.051
Go, go! Go, Alberto! Go!

00:04:57.968 --> 00:04:59.720
(KIDS SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY)

00:05:05.309 --> 00:05:07.061
(LUCA PANTING HEAVILY)

00:05:09.355 --> 00:05:10.898
(ALL EXCLAIMING)

00:05:10.981 --> 00:05:12.691
-Nope. Whoa...
-(KIDS EXCLAIMING)

00:05:13.484 --> 00:05:14.902
(BREATHING NERVOUSLY)

00:05:15.611 --> 00:05:16.612
(MACHIAVELLI GRUMBLES)

00:05:16.695 --> 00:05:17.696
(SNORING)

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:19.073
-MASSIMO: Buongiorno!
-(GASPS)

00:05:19.156 --> 00:05:20.574
(COMMANDS IN ITALIAN)

00:05:22.451 --> 00:05:23.702
(GRUNTING)

00:05:25.496 --> 00:05:27.164
MASSIMO: Sea monster! (GRUNTS)

00:05:27.957 --> 00:05:28.958
(SIGHS)

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:30.334
Whew.

00:05:31.627 --> 00:05:33.087
Oh. (GRUNTS NERVOUSLY)

00:05:35.339 --> 00:05:36.340
DANIELA: Wha...

00:05:36.423 --> 00:05:37.508
LORENZO: Ugo?

00:05:43.556 --> 00:05:44.932
-Rise and shine!
-(BOYS SNORING)

00:05:45.015 --> 00:05:46.892
Only two days till the race.

00:05:47.184 --> 00:05:48.185
Hmm.

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:50.980
Espresso.

00:05:51.063 --> 00:05:52.273
(BOYS GROAN)

00:05:52.356 --> 00:05:53.357
(BOYS GASP)

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:55.109
(BOYS BREATHING HEAVILY)

00:05:56.110 --> 00:05:57.236
Go, Luca!

00:05:57.319 --> 00:05:58.320
Go, go!

00:05:58.571 --> 00:06:00.072
-Hey, don't cheer for him!
-(ALL GASP)

00:06:00.156 --> 00:06:01.157
(COMMANDS IN ITALIAN)

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:03.159
Ha-ha! Whoo!

00:06:04.201 --> 00:06:06.203
(CHUCKLES) This is fun!

00:06:06.287 --> 00:06:08.038
-(MAN SHOUTS IN ITALIAN)
-Uh...

00:06:08.664 --> 00:06:09.707
MASSIMO: Hmm.

00:06:13.085 --> 00:06:14.086
Mm?

00:06:17.256 --> 00:06:18.507
Huh. Hey!

00:06:18.591 --> 00:06:20.301
(LAUGHS) That's amazing!

00:06:20.384 --> 00:06:21.427
(BOTH LAUGH)

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:22.720
-LUCA: Oh, wow!
-(ALBERTO GRUNTS)

00:06:27.308 --> 00:06:29.143
-(KID GASPS)
-(DANIELA SIGHS)

00:06:29.226 --> 00:06:32.521
I don't know, Lorenzo.
Was I too hard on him?

00:06:32.605 --> 00:06:35.941
No. You were just trying
to keep him safe.

00:06:36.233 --> 00:06:37.318
It's my fault.

00:06:37.401 --> 00:06:40.446
I wasn't paying enough attention to him.

00:06:40.529 --> 00:06:43.741
But I was the one who tried
to send him away. (SIGHS)

00:06:43.824 --> 00:06:45.910
I just never in a million years

00:06:45.993 --> 00:06:47.328
would have thought he'd do this.

00:06:47.411 --> 00:06:48.412
It's like I don't even know...

00:06:48.496 --> 00:06:49.497
GIULIA: You can do it, Luca!

00:06:50.414 --> 00:06:51.707
...who he is!

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:53.083
-(GASPS)
-GIULIA: Go, go!

00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:54.418
DANIELA: Luca!
LORENZO: Luca!

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:55.961
DANIELA: Luca, stop!

00:06:57.296 --> 00:06:58.297
Luca!

00:06:59.965 --> 00:07:01.050
(LUCA SIGHS)

00:07:01.133 --> 00:07:02.301
Where are we going?

00:07:02.384 --> 00:07:03.928
Uh... A shortcut.

00:07:04.011 --> 00:07:06.430
Steeper, rough terrain... I like it.

00:07:06.597 --> 00:07:08.224
Why aren't you training?

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:10.226
(MOUTH FULL) I'm always training.

